{
 "probe": "ticket 0001 — old (resident JS) versus new (SQLite/FTS5) on ONE corpus",
 "why_this_is_like_for_like": "Both backends read the same 360 811 passages, produced by a single local-API crawl (7 541 items, fulltext on, 200 000 chars/item). The SQLite side is that crawl's own search-index.json migrated in place, so the corpora are not merely comparable, they are the same rows. This removes the caveat 0001 recorded — that a comparison run through two backends measures the API's differences as well as the index's — and the caveat STATE carried, that no strictly comparable at-rest pair existed: the JSON backend cannot reach 477 512 passages, but both backends reach 360 811.",
